ctly where the two meet.", "keys": [{"lat": 48.25, "lon": -115.75, "d": 30, "az": 180, "el": 24, "cap": "Gibson's palette: Precambrian Belt argillites and quartzites \u2014 the same stack that builds Glacier Park."}, {"lat": 48.28, "lon": -115.66, "d": 14, "az": 210, "el": 16, "cap": "Granite stocks in warm pink \u2014 the Dry Creek and Vermilion intrusions that drove hot fluids through the rock."}, {"lat": 48.21, "lon": -115.57, "d": 12, "az": 140, "el": 15, "cap": "The vein symbols cluster along contacts and faults; each number keys to the mines list printed beside the map."}, {"lat": 48.06, "lon": -115.68, "d": 22, "az": 190, "el": 18, "cap": "South rim of the sheet \u2014 the Vermilion country, prospected hard and rarely rich."}]}, {"id": "rainy", "name": "Rainy Creek", "blurb": "Past the sheet's east edge, an alkaline stock carries vermiculite \u2014 and Libby's long reckoning.", "keys": [{"lat": 48.44, "lon": -115.5, "d": 16, "az": 120, "el": 16, "cap": "Northeast of town, Rainy Creek drains an odd alkaline intrusion \u2014 mined for vermiculite from the 1920s."}, {"lat": 48.462, "lon": -115.437, "d": 10, "az": 100, "el": 14, "cap": "Vermiculite Mountain. The ore that insulated America's attics carried tremolite asbestos; Libby's miners and their families are still paying for it."}, {"lat": 48.41, "lon": -115.49, "d": 14, "az": 200, "el": 15, "cap": "The 1948 sheet records the workings without a word of warning \u2014 no one had written that word yet."}, {"lat": 48.3885, "lon": -115.556, "d": 18, "az": 90, "el": 16, "cap": "Back down to town: company, courthouse, clinic \u2014 and a map that only ever told the geology."}]}], "mines": [{"n": "Alpine Placer", "u": 0.86984, "v": 0.59083, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "American Kootenai", "u": 0.79313, "v": 0.81312, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Big Cherry Creek Placer", "u": 0.76844, "v": 0.52611, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Big Eight", "u": 0.15941, "v": 0.20659, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Big Sky", "u": 0.62218, "v": 0.52897, "c": "lead"}, {"